       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled metformin dose is 2,550 mg/day for IR, and 2,000 mg/day for ER in most labeling.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 to 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 to 850 mg PO two or three times daily**, titrated up from a lower starting dose\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
