       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Nothing in the patient's profile (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) supports exceeding that limit, and the risk of serious harm, especially lactic acidosis, is high. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose with titration, for example 500 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a transcription error or a different formulation, please talk with the pharmacy or your attending first. The order can then be entered through whatever channel your hospital uses for dose-limit overrides.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
